\[x \cdot r^3 = x \cdot \left( \frac{3 - \sqrt{5}}{2} \right)^3 = (9 - 4 \sqrt{5}) x.\]The smallest $t$ such that $\arcsin (\sin tx) = (9 - 4 \sqrt{5}) x$ is $t = \boxed{9 - 4 \sqrt{5}},$ and this is the smallest possible value of $t.$

